  "id": "Compound::DB01110 - Gene::1571",
  "verbalization": "Miconazole appears to interact with Cyp2e1 through a mechanism involving arachidonic acid monooxygenase activity, as evidenced by its binding to Cyp2a6 and Cyp2b6, which in turn participate in this enzymatic process. The shared involvement of Cyp2e1 in arachidonic acid monooxygenase activity suggests a potential role in the metabolic activation of Miconazole, particularly through its resemblance to other antifungal agents like Isoconazole and Tioconazole. This resemblance leads to a binding interaction with Cyp2e1, which may contribute to the drug's antifungal effects by modulating the activity of cytochrome P450 enzymes involved in the metabolism of imidazole antifungal drugs. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible dependency on Cyp2e1 for the metabolic activation of Miconazole, particularly in the context of antifungal action.",
